1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,750
From Personnel, select Manage Invites.

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:07,489
The Invites page separates the invitation
history from the Send Invites form.

3
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:12,239
Its history has Email Address, Sent On and
Completed On columns.

4
00:00:12,699 --> 00:00:16,540
This walkthrough invites a fictional new
member, Derrick Gibson, and

5
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,530
verifies the result from both sides.

6
00:00:18,959 --> 00:00:22,250
An invitation is useful when a new team
member should complete

7
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:25,780
their own account details instead of an
administrator entering every

8
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,450
credential through Add a Person.

9
00:00:27,629 --> 00:00:30,510
Enter the intended recipient in Email
Addresses.

10
00:00:30,959 --> 00:00:34,799
The help explains that multiple addresses
can be separated by commas.

11
00:00:35,279 --> 00:00:38,539
This exercise uses a single fictional
training address.

12
00:00:38,959 --> 00:00:42,049
Review the destination and select Send
Invites.

13
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:46,309
The saved row then shows the address, a
Sent On time and

14
00:00:46,309 --> 00:00:47,970
Pending under Completed On.

15
00:00:48,479 --> 00:00:50,659
Check that row for the intended recipient.

16
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:55,120
Pending is an invitation state; it does
not establish that the recipient

17
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:56,860
has finished joining the department.

18
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:01,059
While the invitation is pending, the row
offers Resend Invite.

19
00:01:01,429 --> 00:01:04,940
If delivery needs another attempt, review
the intended address

20
00:01:04,999 --> 00:01:08,300
and confirm that the recipient actually
receives the invitation.

21
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:12,920
Here the controlled local Mailpit inbox
contains the Resgrid invitation

22
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,029
for the training department.

23
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:18,080
Opening that email shows the inviting
administrator, the department

24
00:01:18,359 --> 00:01:19,949
and a Set up account button.

25
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:24,900
This mailbox is our local recording tool;
your members use their own mailbox.

26
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,779
Follow Set up account to the registration
form.

27
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:31,869
The invitation link itself is private and
is not shown in this lesson.

28
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:35,270
The form identifies the department the
recipient is joining.

29
00:01:35,699 --> 00:01:40,269
Enter the member’s own name, a unique
Username, and matching password fields.

30
00:01:40,659 --> 00:01:44,920
Our fictional example is Derrick Gibson,
and the passwords remain masked.

31
00:01:45,239 --> 00:01:48,530
The displayed password requirement is at
least eight characters,

32
00:01:48,659 --> 00:01:52,309
including a digit, an uppercase letter and
a lowercase letter.

33
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:56,950
Review the terms of use and privacy policy
notice before Register, because

34
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,909
signing up accepts those terms.

35
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:02,530
The notice also describes existing-account
linking, but this

36
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:04,969
exercise creates a new fictional account.

37
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:07,469
Select Register after that review.

38
00:02:07,709 --> 00:02:10,719
The returned workspace is signed in as
Derrick Gibson.

39
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:14,739
Check the name at the upper left and the
intended department in the header.

40
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:18,700
That visible signed-in result is stronger
evidence than assuming

41
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:19,969
the Register button worked.

42
00:02:20,379 --> 00:02:24,249
The new member now has a department
workspace in this local exercise.

43
00:02:24,659 --> 00:02:28,239
Operational status and staffing controls
are separate from accepting

44
00:02:28,239 --> 00:02:32,739
the invitation; no responding status or
staffing change is performed here.

45
00:02:32,950 --> 00:02:36,159
Return to Manage Invites under the
administrator account.

46
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:39,780
The same recipient now has an actual
Completed On date

47
00:02:39,809 --> 00:02:41,499
and time rather than Pending.

48
00:02:41,850 --> 00:02:43,840
Sent On remains a separate value.

49
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:47,220
Compare those two columns when checking
whether an invitation

50
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:49,339
was merely sent or was completed.

51
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:53,890
In this recorded example, completion is
saved at seventeen fifteen and

52
00:02:53,890 --> 00:02:56,189
fifty-six seconds on the displayed date.

53
00:02:56,539 --> 00:03:00,820
This administrative readback confirms the
completed invitation independently

54
00:03:00,849 --> 00:03:02,390
of the member’s signed-in page.

55
00:03:02,650 --> 00:03:06,069
Open Personnel and use Search to find
Derrick Gibson.

56
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:10,910
The saved row shows Normal under State,
Available under Staffing

57
00:03:11,169 --> 00:03:13,080
and Standing By under Status.

58
00:03:13,459 --> 00:03:16,299
Roles is still blank for this newly
invited member.

59
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:20,289
Review the department group and
operational role the person needs as

60
00:03:20,289 --> 00:03:22,279
part of your own onboarding process.

61
00:03:22,639 --> 00:03:26,010
The member-access walkthrough demonstrates
those separate controls.

62
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:30,150
This invitation exercise verifies
membership without granting a

63
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:33,859
department administrator role or assigning
an operational role.

64
00:03:34,029 --> 00:03:38,420
Use the same invitation and verification
process for community paramedicine

65
00:03:38,489 --> 00:03:42,800
and mental health response teams,
search-and-rescue organizations, security

66
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:47,310
departments, wildland contractors and
industrial emergency teams, as

67
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,470
well as fire and E M S departments.

68
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:54,409
Send to the intended recipient, verify
delivery, let the member complete

69
00:03:54,409 --> 00:03:57,870
the form, and check the completed
invitation and personnel row.

70
00:03:58,309 --> 00:04:02,280
Those readbacks help administrators
distinguish an outstanding invitation

71
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,340
from a member who has actually joined.

